+## Optional: write your own rows into a release-gate ledger
+
+When this run is part of a `release-gate` sequence and the gate supplied `--gate-ledger <run-dir>`,
+append your rows as you finish instead of waiting for the gate to copy them:
+
+```
+node "<gate-skill-dir>/scripts/gate_record.mjs" lane <run-dir> --lane perf --target <host> --verdict <v> --sha <git-head>
+```
+
+Your verdict stays in your own vocabulary (measured / not-measured). The ledger never translates it, and nothing here
+adds a check, a severity or a request to this skill.
+
+One row per finding (`--id PERF-<nn>`, plus route, severity, remediation and the evidence reference from
+Finding record) and a `--touches` value of `data`, `money`, `role`, `none` or `unknown` — whether
+the finding reaches another user's data, money or role boundary. Fill it from what the finding
+actually says; `none` is a claim, not a default.
+
+Without `--gate-ledger` nothing changes: report as usual and let the gate copy your table.
